==============================================================================
S8 (b) -- COSTING THE FIX.  Fact 644: cost is not a design constraint.
==============================================================================
  S7 PR19 disaggregated says K1's noise-null failure is VARIANCE on
  62-frame stacks.  Variance averages down; bias does not.  So the
  honest expensive proposal is to average independent ROIs.

  PREMISE (ARGUED, UNMEASURED -- this is section 11 item 2): the
  per-ROI scatter falls as 1/sqrt(N) across disjoint 512^2 ROIs.
  If ROIs share scene structure or fixed-pattern noise it will not.
  The table below is the COST OF THE TEST, not a result.

  cell                     sd/ROI    N@0.10    N@0.05    N@0.02    N@0.01
  --------------------------------------------------------------
  109MSDCF/centre          0.0823         1         3        17        68
  112MSDCF/detail          0.0305         1         1         3        10
  112MSDCF/flat            0.0584         1         2         9        35

  Worst measured cell needs 17 disjoint 512^2 ROIs for a 0.02 px
  threshold.  A 6000x4000 frame holds ~91 disjoint 512^2 tiles, so this
  is one to two frames' worth of area -- affordable under fact 644, and
  it is the experiment this milestone did not run.

